  "_comment": "Channel presets for the dashboard Streams page. Bind-mounted read-only and re-read on every GET /presets, so edits apply without a container restart (a repo commit + deploy is what makes them durable). Groups: organizers = official tournament broadcasts on Twitch (the ones HLTV links from match pages), kick = the same organizers' Kick channels, streamers = popular CS2 personalities, youtube = channels that go live on YouTube (watch URL is https://www.youtube.com/@<channel>/live). EVERY handle here was resolved against the platform before being added (Twitch GQL user lookup / Kick channel API, 2026-09-18) — a handle existing is not enough, it also has to be the organizer's real channel. Two entries were removed in that pass: 'blasttv' did not exist at all, and 'fissure' was a 346-follower placeholder that has never broadcast, not FISSURE the organizer. Name-matching is genuinely unsafe here: 'esltv' is ESL's Dota channel, and 'thunderpick', 'cct', 'nodwin', 'united21', 'esnation' and 'eslproleague' are all squatted handles with ~0 followers.",
